  "purpose": "Improve visual grounding, conversational Korean and named-term fidelity while preserving the fixed OCR slot ownership established by e64b6831.",
  "implementation": [
    "Keep the existing original whole-page image. Read scene context before translating each fixed bbox; clear visible lettering may correct ko despite OCR errors, without rewriting saved source, IDs, geometry or grouping.",
    "Prioritize visible furigana and established/user-corrected terminology; avoid borrowing neighboring text or inventing missing letters from genre expectations.",
    "Clarify colloquial intent, idioms, kana word boundaries, relationships and names, with Korean guidance for Japanese-to-Korean translation.",
    "Reject linguistic expansion of six-or-more digit-only Hayai ordinary slots, including readable/advisory fallbacks. Retry only the affected slot and preserve source with needs_review when repairs fail. Short counts and legacy non-Hayai slots retain their prior policy."
  ],
